from cursor to next word start', ' Type the characters that should replace what you typed at the previous prompt, and press Enter.', 'If you have selected text with the mark and then search to replace, only matches in the selected text will be replaced.', 'Run the last recorded macro', 'Search backward for a string', ' The nano editor is designed to emulate the functionality and ease-of-use of the UW Pico text editor.  There are four main sections of the editor.  The top line shows the program version, the current filename being edited, and whether or not the file has been modified.  Next is the main editor window showing the file being edited.  The status line is the third line from the bottom and shows important messages.  ', 'Place or remove an anchor at the current line', 'operatingdir', '%s                ', ':d3', ' The previous search string will be shown in brackets after the search prompt.  Hitting Enter without entering any text will perform the previous search.', '=== Linter ===', 'Write File Help Text', 'Cut current line (or marked region) and store it in cutbuffer', 'magic', 'Toggle the case sensitivity of the search', 'Go to lefthand column', ' If you have compiled nano with multiple file buffer support, and enable multiple file buffers with the -F or --multibuffer command line flags, the Meta-F toggle, or a nanorc file, inserting a file will cause it to be loaded into a separate buffer (use Meta-< and > to switch between file buffers).  ', 'Search next occurrence forward', '0nR', 'Go to previous line', ' The file browser is used to visually browse the directory structure to select a file for reading or writing.  You may use the arrow keys or Page Up/Down to browse through the files, and S or Enter to choose the selected file or enter the selected directory.  To move up one level, select the directory called ".." at the top of the file list.', 'Go to righthand column', 'Toggle the use of a new buffer', '(%s)       ', 'Delete backward from cursor to word start', ' The following function keys are available in Write File mode:', '%*zd', 'Go back one word', 'Mark text starting from the cursor position', 'Welcome to nano.  For basic help, type Ctrl+G.', ' Type in the name of a file to be inserted into the current file buffer at the current cursor location.', 'Help', 'Go to the next file in the list', 'Scroll down one line without moving the cursor textually', 'Go to end of current line', 'Close buffer without saving it', " Shortcuts are written as follows: Control-key sequences are notated with a '^' and can be entered either by using the Ctrl key or pressing the Esc key twice.  Meta-key sequences are notated with 'M-' and can be entered using either the Alt, Cmd, or Esc key, depending on your keyboard setup.  ", '/usr/share/locale', 'Go to the first line of the file', 'Cancel the current function', '%s\t\t %s %s', 'Toggle appending', 'Toggle the use of Mac format', 'Insert another file into current buffer (or into new buffer)', 'Go to next line', ' If you have selected text with the mark, you will be prompted to save only the selected portion to a separate file.  To reduce the chance of overwriting the current file with just a portion of it, the current filename is not the default in this mode.', 'File Browser Help Text', "Can't go outside of %s", 'Write the current buffer (or the marked region) to disk', 'Show line numbers in front of the text', 'Go to the matching bracket', 'Go to the previous file in the list', 'Delete the character under the cursor', 'Search backward for a string or a regular expression', '- R', 'Insert a newline at the cursor position', 'Browser Search Command Help Text', 'B?@', 'Do not convert from DOS/Mac format', ' Enter the line number that you wish to go to and hit Enter.  If there are fewer lines of text than the number you entered, you will be brought to the last line of the file.', 'Scroll up one line without moving the cursor textually', 'Paste the contents of cutbuffer at current cursor position', ' If tab completion has not been disabled, you can use the Tab key to (attempt to) automatically complete the directory name.', 'B/D', 'Go to first row in the viewport', 'Also try magic to determine syntax', 'Copy current line (or marked region) and store it in cutbuffer', ' You can also pick one of four tools, or cut a large piece of the buffer, or put the editor to sleep.', "Can't write outside of %s", 'Toggle the use of DOS format', "Can't read file from outside of %s", 'Toggle the use of regular expressions', 'Go to last row in this column', 'Execute a function or an external command', 'bindtextdomain', 'stpcpy', 'If you need another blank buffer, do not enter any filename, or type in a nonexistent filename at the prompt and press Enter.', 'Main nano help text', '\t`B', ' The following function keys are available in Browser Go To Directory mode:', 'Jump backward to the nearest anchor', ' The following function keys are available in Go To Line mode:', '0C L&', 'Switch to the previous file buffer', 'Go one screenful up']
