postive strings [" This mode allows you to insert the output of a command run by the shell into the current buffer (or into a new buffer).  If the command is preceded by '|' (the pipe symbol), the current contents of the buffer (or marked region) will be piped to the command.  ", 'Set operating directory', 'Start/stop recording a macro', 'Insert a tab at the cursor position (or indent marked lines)', 'Toggle backing up of the original file', '\t\t  %s', '--magic', ' The following function keys are available in the file browser:', 'Execute Command Help Text', 'Search forward for a string', 'dcgettext', ' In this mode, the status bar shows an error message or warning, and the cursor is put at the corresponding position in the file.  With PageUp and PageDown you can switch to earlier and later messages.', '300', 'Go to beginning of current line', 'Undo the last operation', 'Go to line and column number', 'dcngettext', 'Close the current buffer / Exit from nano', 'Redo the last undone operation', 'Go back one character', 'Jump forward to the nearest anchor', 'Go to file browser', 'Invalid operating directory: %s', ' The following function keys are available at this prompt:', '=== Replacement ===', 'Push the cursor line to the center, then top, then bottom', '--operatingdir=<dir>', 'linenumbers', 'Also, pressing Esc twice and then typing a three-digit decimal number from 000 to 255 will enter the character with the corresponding value.  The following keystrokes are available in the main editor window.  Alternative keys are shown in parentheses:', 'Replace a string or a regular expression', 'Go to the last line of the file', 'Throw away the current line (or marked region)', 'M-#', 'Center the line where the cursor is', 'Suspend the editor (return to the shell)', 'Insert File Help Text', ' --disable-wrapping', 'Go to last row in the viewport', 'Save file without prompting', ' The following function keys are available in Search mode:', 'A0D', 'Search Command Help Text', '-o <dir>', 'Go to directory', 'Pipe the current buffer (or marked region) to the command', 'Display this help text', ' The following function keys are available in Linter mode:', 'Go to the first file in the list', 'Search forward for a string or a regular expression', '*}b', 'Display the position of the cursor', 'Go forward one word', ' The following function keys are available in Insert File mode:', 'Exit from the file browser', 'Go To Line Help Text', 'Refresh (redraw) the current screen', ' Enter the name of the directory you would like to browse to.', ' Enter the words or characters you would like to search for, and then press Enter.  If there is a match for the text you entered, the screen will be updated to the location of the nearest match for the search string.', 'Indent the current line (or marked lines)', 'If you just need another blank buffer, do not enter any command.', 'Go forward one character', 'Reverse the direction of the search', 'Count the number of lines, words, and characters', 'chdir', 'Switch to the next file buffer', 'Unindent the current line (or marked lines)', 'Go to first row in this column', ' The previous search string will be shown in brackets after the search prompt.  Hitting Enter without entering any text will perform the previous search.  ', 'Browser Go To Directory Help Text', 'p,4', 'Go to next block of text', 'Go to the last file in the list', '(pg', 'Insert the next keystroke verbatim', '--linenumbers', 'Refresh the file list', 'Cut from the cursor position to the end of the file', 'Search next occurrence backward', 'Delete the character to the left of the cursor', ' Type the name that you wish to save the current file as and press Enter to save the file.', 'Go to previous block of text', 'Toggle prepending', 'The bottom two lines show the most commonly used shortcuts in the editor.', 'enable/disable', 'nano', 'Go one screenful down', 'Delete forward from cursor to next word start', ' Type the characters that should replace what you typed at the previous prompt, and press Enter.', 'If you have selected text with the mark and then search to replace, only matches in the selected text will be replaced.', 'Run the last recorded macro', 'Search backward for a string', ' The nano editor is designed to emulate the functionality and ease-of-use of the UW Pico text editor.  There are four main sections of the editor.  The top line shows the program version, the current filename being edited, and whether or not the file has been modified.  Next is the main editor window showing the file being edited.  The status line is the third line from the bottom and shows important messages.  ', 'Place or remove an anchor at the current line', 'operatingdir', '%s                ', ':d3', ' The previous search string will be shown in brackets after the search prompt.  Hitting Enter without entering any text will perform the previous search.', '=== Linter ===', 'Write File Help Text', 'Cut current line (or marked region) and store it in cutbuffer', 'magic', 'Toggle the case sensitivity of the search', 'Go to lefthand column', ' If you have compiled nano with multiple file buffer support, and enable multiple file buffers with the -F or --multibuffer command line flags, the Meta-F toggle, or a nanorc file, inserting a file will cause it to be loaded into a separate buffer (use Meta-< and > to switch between file buffers).  ', 'Search next occurrence forward', '0nR', 'Go to previous line', ' The file browser is used to visually browse the directory structure to select a file for reading or writing.  You may use the arrow keys or Page Up/Down to browse through the files, and S or Enter to choose the selected file or enter the selected directory.  To move up one level, select the directory called ".." at the top of the file list.', 'Go to righthand column', 'Toggle the use of a new buffer', '(%s)       ', 'Delete backward from cursor to word start', ' The following function keys are available in Write File mode:', '%*zd', 'Go back one word', 'Mark text starting from the cursor position', 'Welcome to nano.  For basic help, type Ctrl+G.', ' Type in the name of a file to be inserted into the current file buffer at the current cursor location.', 'Help', 'Go to the next file in the list', 'Scroll down one line without moving the cursor textually', 'Go to end of current line', 'Close buffer without saving it', " Shortcuts are written as follows: Control-key sequences are notated with a '^' and can be entered either by using the Ctrl key or pressing the Esc key twice.  Meta-key sequences are notated with 'M-' and can be entered using either the Alt, Cmd, or Esc key, depending on your keyboard setup.  ", '/usr/share/locale', 'Go to the first line of the file', 'Cancel the current function', '%s\t\t %s %s', 'Toggle appending', 'Toggle the use of Mac format', 'Insert another file into current buffer (or into new buffer)', 'Go to next line', ' If you have selected text with the mark, you will be prompted to save only the selected portion to a separate file.  To reduce the chance of overwriting the current file with just a portion of it, the current filename is not the default in this mode.', 'File Browser Help Text', "Can't go outside of %s", 'Write the current buffer (or the marked region) to disk', 'Show line numbers in front of the text', 'Go to the matching bracket', 'Go to the previous file in the list', 'Delete the character under the cursor', 'Search backward for a string or a regular expression', '- R', 'Insert a newline at the cursor position', 'Browser Search Command Help Text', 'B?@', 'Do not convert from DOS/Mac format', ' Enter the line number that you wish to go to and hit Enter.  If there are fewer lines of text than the number you entered, you will be brought to the last line of the file.', 'Scroll up one line without moving the cursor textually', 'Paste the contents of cutbuffer at current cursor position', ' If tab completion has not been disabled, you can use the Tab key to (attempt to) automatically complete the directory name.', 'B/D', 'Go to first row in the viewport', 'Also try magic to determine syntax', 'Copy current line (or marked region) and store it in cutbuffer', ' You can also pick one of four tools, or cut a large piece of the buffer, or put the editor to sleep.', "Can't write outside of %s", 'Toggle the use of DOS format', "Can't read file from outside of %s", 'Toggle the use of regular expressions', 'Go to last row in this column', 'Execute a function or an external command', 'bindtextdomain', 'stpcpy', 'If you need another blank buffer, do not enter any filename, or type in a nonexistent filename at the prompt and press Enter.', 'Main nano help text', '\t`B', ' The following function keys are available in Browser Go To Directory mode:', 'Jump backward to the nearest anchor', ' The following function keys are available in Go To Line mode:', '0C L&', 'Switch to the previous file buffer', 'Go one screenful up']
